WEBVTT

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:09.935
A help desk can use different rules to prepare labels.

00:00:09.935 --> 00:00:13.210
We will pass each rule to the same rendering method,

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:14.784
then compare the results.

00:00:31.932 --> 00:00:35.080
A functional interface has one abstract method

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.722
describing an operation.

00:00:36.722 --> 00:00:40.212
Here, Function takes a String and returns a String.

00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:43.223
Its first type argument describes the input.

00:00:43.223 --> 00:00:45.413
The second describes the result.

00:00:45.413 --> 00:00:48.560
LabelPrinter receives the rule as an argument.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:51.982
Calling apply runs that supplied rule on the text.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.949
A lambda expression supplies behavior using parameters

00:00:55.949 --> 00:00:56.688
and a body.

00:00:56.688 --> 00:00:58.570
Here, text is the parameter.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:01.460
The expression after the arrow is the body.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.350
Creating the lambda does not run that body.

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.844
A method reference supplies compatible behavior from

00:01:07.844 --> 00:01:09.121
an existing method.

00:01:09.121 --> 00:01:12.280
String colon colon trim uses trim on the String

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.960
supplied when apply runs.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.320
Trim removes spaces from the ends of these inputs.

00:01:17.399 --> 00:01:19.380
Predict the three output lines.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.574
Which rule does each call pass, and when does that

00:01:22.574 --> 00:01:23.149
rule run?

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.874
Pause here before checking.

00:01:29.673 --> 00:01:33.188
The first line is Maya, with the surrounding spaces

00:01:33.188 --> 00:01:33.739
removed.

00:01:33.739 --> 00:01:37.323
The tag rule adds Guest, a colon, and a space before

00:01:37.323 --> 00:01:37.668
Luis.

00:01:37.668 --> 00:01:41.252
The method reference removes the spaces around Nora.

00:01:41.252 --> 00:01:44.905
Each render call invokes apply, so the same rendering

00:01:44.905 --> 00:01:47.248
method can use different behavior.

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:51.012
Change only the tag lambda so it puts square brackets

00:01:51.012 --> 00:01:52.113
around its input.

00:01:52.113 --> 00:01:55.157
Predict the second output line, then run again.

00:01:55.157 --> 00:01:58.395
Which other output lines should stay the same, and

00:01:58.395 --> 00:01:58.654
why?
